# Extension Development Rules

## Stack

- WXT + TypeScript + Manifest V3
- Entrypoints in `apps/extension/src/entrypoints/`
- Shared logic in `apps/extension/src/lib/`

## Entrypoints

- `background.ts` — service worker; side panel registration, message relay, reading-tab pinning
- `content.ts` — runs in page context; DOM wrapping and charIndex highlighting
- `sidepanel/` — user UI; speech controls and settings

## Messaging

Use typed messages from `lib/messages.ts`. Pattern:

```typescript
// side panel → background → content script
chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ type: "GET_PAGE_READING" });
```

Content script returns `{ type: "PAGE_READING", text, title }` or `{ type: "ERROR", message }`.

Highlight flow (speechify-dry-run pattern):
- `{ type: "HIGHLIGHT_AT_CHAR", charIndex }` — word highlight at global char index
- `{ type: "CLEAR_HIGHLIGHT" }` — clear highlight styles only
- `{ type: "TEARDOWN_READING" }` — unwrap DOM spans after stop/end

Speech runs in the side panel via `SpeechReader.speakText()` (single utterance); highlighting runs in the content script.

## Storage

User preferences in `chrome.storage.local`:
- Key: `geordi:speech-settings`
- Shape: `{ voiceURI: string | null, rate: number }`

## Permissions

Current: `activeTab`, `sidePanel`, `storage`, `scripting`, `<all_urls>` host permission for content scripts.

Do not add permissions without justification in an ADR.

## Build

```bash
pnpm dev:ext    # development
pnpm build:ext  # production
```

Output: `apps/extension/.output/`
